  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "An acidified solution of potassium chromate was layered with an equal volume of amyl alcohol. When it was shaken after the addition of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>%</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></math> a blue alcohol layer was obtained. The blue color is due to the formation of a chromium (VI) compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math>. What is the number of oxygen atoms bonded to chromium through only single bonds in a molecule of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math>?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CrO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mover><mo>→</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mover><munder><msub><mi>CrO</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>Deep</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi>Blue</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi>solution</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></munder></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/8736a1ea-2395-486d-9bc9-3de7c455ab54-image.png\"/></p><p>No. of oxygen atom bonded with chromium with single bond is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p><p> </p>",
    "image": null
  },
